From: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 12:19:11 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] AP MLD: advertise TID-to-link mapping negotiation support

hostapd_eid_eht_basic_ml_common() clears the TID-To-Link Mapping
Negotiation Support subfield of the MLD capabilities that the driver
gives, since the AP MLD did not answer a negotiation.

Advertise the value of the driver where the driver applies a negotiated
mapping (NL80211_EXT_FEATURE_AP_NEG_TTLM). A driver can set the
subfield for its AP interface type without that support, and the value
2 is reserved, so both still give 0.

Signed-off-by: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
Signed-off-by: ViKing <viking.yfy@qq.com>

--- a/src/ap/ieee802_11_eht.c
+++ b/src/ap/ieee802_11_eht.c
@@ -529,8 +529,8 @@
 	mld_cap &= ~EHT_ML_MLD_CAPA_MAX_NUM_SIM_LINKS_MASK;
 	mld_cap |= active_links & EHT_ML_MLD_CAPA_MAX_NUM_SIM_LINKS_MASK;
 
-	/* TODO: Advertise T2LM based on driver support as well */
 	mld_cap &= ~EHT_ML_MLD_CAPA_TID_TO_LINK_MAP_NEG_SUPP_MSK;
+	mld_cap |= hostapd_mld_neg_ttlm_capa(hapd);
 
 	mld_cap |= EHT_ML_MLD_CAPA_LINK_RECONF_OP_SUPPORT;
 
